<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ante Pavelić</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1889–1959</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ante Pavelić was the founder of the fascist <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ustase">Ustaše</a> movement and leader, as Poglavnik, of the Independent State of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/croatia">Croatia</a> from 1941 to 1945. His regime, an <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/axis-powers">Axis</a> puppet state, carried out <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/genocide">genocide</a> against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/serbs">Serbs</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jews">Jews</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/romani-people">Roma</a>, including at the Jasenovac camp. He fled in 1945 and died in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a> after surviving an assassination attempt in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/argentina">Argentina</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ante-pavelic.jpg" alt="Ante Pavelić" width="320" height="429" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Willy Pragher · CC BY 3.0 de · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Ante_Paveli%C4%87_StAF_(3x4_cropped).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
